### MPSCALC-300 (built here). MEASURED at drafting: Backlog, labels `lane-v5 mpscalc-b340 plan-b340-b319-3 tier-2`, 0 links, 0 comments, updated 2026-10-20.
- Title: "[B319-3] Quantity audit: a purchase section with more than one device line reads as noise, every device line flagged as not 1 per device". Finding: in a purchase section the audit counts all device lines as D, so two device lines of eight and four both read as a quantity for twelve devices and both are flagged "not 1 per device". "That is the literal R-V5-1 rule, and it reads as noise until sections become single-model groups." Recommendation (verbatim shape): decide the rule for a section with several device lines, "for example flag per device line, or do not flag a multi-device section, or wait for single-model groups ... Then change isFlagged and purchaseAudit." The ticket says it "waits on a coordinator decision, not on a card the product owner has not ruled".
- **Acceptance check, verbatim:** "The section test with two device lines (different quantities) expects the ruled reading, and a single-device section is unchanged."
- **THE COORDINATOR'S DECISION (this kit's reading; binding, said once):** *flag a line only when its per-device quantity is not 1 AND the section has one device line; with more device lines, show the quantity unflagged. The flag is advisory, blocks nothing, changes no price.* It is the ticket's second named option ("do not flag a multi-device section"). **It fits the ticket (MEASURED, `web/src/screens/bom/quantityAuditModel.ts` at main `3496da33`):** `purchaseAudit` (:95-106) sums the quantity of every non-credit, non-optional line whose resolved class is `device` into `devices` (:99), reads each line's `perDeviceOf(quantity, devices)` (:101) and sets `flagged: isFlagged(itemClass, per)` (:102), so with device lines of 8 and 4, `devices` is 12 and each reads `partial` (8 for 12, 4 for 12) and is flagged: the ticket's example, exactly. The ruled reading changes only the `flagged` value, in the case of two or more counted device lines. **If, at your base, the file or the render no longer fits this description, that is a STOP at this item with a Q for Tuesday.**
- **WHAT "SHOW THE QUANTITY UNFLAGGED" MEANS (MEASURED, `web/src/screens/bom/QuantityAudit.tsx` :113-122 at main):** each audit row already shows `Qty` (`l.quantity`) and a `Per device` cell (`perDeviceText(l.per)`, for example "8 for 12 devices"); the only flag is the `Check` cell chip `Not 1 per device` (:120). So "unflagged" = the chip is absent and the quantity and the `Per device` text stay exactly as today. **No new word, no new column, no change to `QuantityAudit.tsx`.**
- **Counted device line (said once; the same set the engine and `devices` use):** a line in the section whose resolved class is `device` and which is neither `credit` nor `optional` (`quantityAuditModel.ts:99`). A credit device line, an optional device line, a line whose catalogue key is not in the inventory (class null) and every non-device line is NOT a counted device line. Two lines of the same SKU are two device lines (the rule counts lines, as the ticket says "device lines").

