## PROPERTY (BINDING, said first; then the minimum)
**General property:** *for every purchase section of every draft, `purchaseAudit` returns the same sections, the same lines in the same order, and for every line the same `lineNumber`, `code`, `itemClass`, `quantity`, `per` and the section the same `sectionId`, `label` and `devices` as at base; the `flagged` value of a line equals base's value when the section has at most one counted device line, and is false for every line of a section with two or more counted device lines; no visible word, no price, no request and no other file changes.*
At least these cases, each a test row (synthetic data only; one section per draft unless stated):
(a) **two device lines of 8 and 4, plus a care pack line of 12** (the ticket's own example): no `Not 1 per device` chip anywhere; both device rows still read "8 for 12 devices" and "4 for 12 devices"; the section caption still reads "12 devices"; the care row still reads "1 per device".
(b) **two device lines (8 and 4) plus a care pack line of 24 and an option line of 5:** the lines that base flags (2 per device, "5 for 12 devices") are unflagged now, all rows keep their `Qty` and `Per device` text.
(c) **one device line of 12 plus a care pack line of 24, and another with 5:** flagged exactly as at base ("2 per device" flagged; "5 for 12 devices" flagged), the device line itself unflagged (12 for 12).
(d) **a credit device line and an optional device line do not count:** one counted device line (12) plus one credit device line (3) plus one optional device line (2) plus a care pack line of 24: the care row is flagged (one counted device line, as at base).
(e) **a line whose key is not in the inventory is not a device line:** one counted device line plus an unknown-key line: unknown row unflagged ("Class not known"), the care row flagged as at base.
(f) **two sections in one draft:** section 1 has one device line and a flagged care line; section 2 has two device lines and a care line that base flags: section 1's flag stays, section 2 has none (the rule is per section, not per draft).
(g) **no counted device line:** lines are listed unflagged and read "No devices in this section", as at base.
(h) **two device lines of the same SKU** count as two device lines.
(i) **seeded sweep with an independent oracle:** a deterministic generator (your own small seeded integer generator, the seed a named constant in the file; no `Math.random`) builds at least 200 sections of 0 to 4 device lines (some credit, some optional, some with unknown keys) and 0 to 5 lines of the other classes, quantities from 1 to 40; for each, the test computes the expected flags from first principles (count the counted device lines; one or none: `isFlagged(class, perDeviceOf(quantity, devices))` imported from the model; two or more: all false) and compares to `purchaseAudit`; it also asserts that the draft object is deep-equal before and after (the audit never changes a quantity) and that the result is the same for the lines in reverse order and rotated by one. The control: a deliberately wrong oracle (flag when the section has MORE than one device line) must fail the same sweep (a row that proves the sweep can fail).
(j) **render rows** for (a), (b) and (f) through `PurchaseQuantityAudit` (the existing tests' way: `render`, the closed block opened by its button), and one row that mounts `PurchaseBomEditor` with a two-device-line draft (as the existing mount row does) and asserts `onChange` is not called and no `alert` exists (advisory: blocks nothing).
Any other shape: prove it meets the property or STOP.

